  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, the Mark 93 pattern. The special options position follows the sheet's own rule, combine up to two options in alphabetical order, so the slot enumerates every single and every alphabetical pair; a build with no options assembles with a trailing dash here, and whether the factory prints the bare form without it is held for John. The metric sizes print their own footnote, specify end connection code X, enforced both ways. The X end's own footnote names size options D12 and D18 where the size rows print DN10 and DN15, a naming mismatch held for John. If no gasket is specified the sheet supplies TFE/Viton, and the welded body needs no gasket option, both by the sheet's own notes.",
